    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.8da8539ef1c928b567cc",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "`permissions:type:delegate` scope ensures that users can only assign roles which have same, or a subset of permissions which the user has. For example, if a user does not have required permissions for creating users, they won't be able to assign a role which will allow to do that. This is done to prevent escalation of privileges.",
      "headingPath": [
        "RBAC API",
        "Create and remove service account role assignments",
        "Add a service account role assignment",
        "Required permissions"
      ],
      "source": {
