    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.571d98073aa653d2a16a",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "`permissions:type:delegate` scope ensures that users can only assign roles which have same, or a subset of permissions which the user has. For example, if a user does not have the permissions required to create users, they won't be able to assign a role that contains these permissions. This is done to prevent escalation of privileges.",
      "headingPath": [
