    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.79ec33aa6e342b76cfb7",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "`permissions:type:delegate` scope ensures that users can only unassign roles which have same, or a subset of permissions which the user has. For example, if a user does not have the permissions required to create users, they won't be able to assign a role that contains these permissions. This is done to prevent escalation of privileges.```",
      "headingPath": [
        "RBAC API",
        "Remove a team role assignment",
        "Required permissions"
      ],
      "source": {
