    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.80711e9b3e3203aa519e",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Grafana supports a variety of different data sources, each with its own data model. To manage this, Grafana consolidates the query results from each of these data sources into one unified data structure called a **data frame**. Additionally, the **data plane** adds a property layer to the data frame with information about the data frame type and what the data frame holds.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Developer tools in Grafana",
        "Data structure in Grafana"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/developer-resources/developer-tools/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "d352379b7e9e03707ade12c89282a613a6fdf0a4",
