    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.34ed77a4327919b9f6e8",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "This _histogram_ shows the value distribution of a couple of time series. You can easily see that most values land between 240-300 with a peak between 260-280.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Introduction to histograms and heatmaps",
        "Histogram example"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/fundamentals/intro-histograms/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "ae9ae70d7cf259aa312df4ed3911fb6863f59187",
        "sha256": "b6c9655954eab2f8d24641192907358c18408bfc0e465ac2466a617555ef6fee",
        "lineStart": 43,
        "lineEnd": 44,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/fundamentals/intro-histograms/index.md#L43-L44"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.8671564b55abf54b8dda",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Histograms only look at _value distributions_ over a specific time range. The problem with histograms is that you cannot see any trends or changes in the distribution over time. This is where heatmaps become useful.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Introduction to histograms and heatmaps",
        "Histogram example"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/fundamentals/intro-histograms/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "ae9ae70d7cf259aa312df4ed3911fb6863f59187",
        "sha256": "b6c9655954eab2f8d24641192907358c18408bfc0e465ac2466a617555ef6fee",
        "lineStart": 54,
        "lineEnd": 54,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/fundamentals/intro-histograms/index.md#L54-L54"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.d0bec83ef766301a8cfc",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "In this example, you can clearly see what values are more common and how they trend over time.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Introduction to histograms and heatmaps",
        "Heatmaps"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/fundamentals/intro-histograms/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "ae9ae70d7cf259aa312df4ed3911fb6863f59187",
        "sha256": "b6c9655954eab2f8d24641192907358c18408bfc0e465ac2466a617555ef6fee",
        "lineStart": 60,
        "lineEnd": 60,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/fundamentals/intro-histograms/index.md#L60-L60"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.e7b1217d41ab849d19ea",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "There are a number of data sources supporting histogram over time, like Elasticsearch (by using a Histogram bucket aggregation) or Prometheus (with [histogram](https://prometheus.io/docs/concepts/metric_types/#histogram) metric type and _Format as_ option set to Heatmap). But generally, any data source could be used as long as it meets the requirement that it either returns series with names representing bucket bounds, or that it returns series sorted by the bounds in ascending order.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Introduction to histograms and heatmaps",
        "Pre-bucketed data"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/fundamentals/intro-histograms/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "ae9ae70d7cf259aa312df4ed3911fb6863f59187",
        "sha256": "b6c9655954eab2f8d24641192907358c18408bfc0e465ac2466a617555ef6fee",
        "lineStart": 68,
        "lineEnd": 72,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/fundamentals/intro-histograms/index.md#L68-L72"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.3ae8eb007c100bd9b21c",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "If you use the heatmap with regular time series data (not pre-bucketed), then it's important to keep in mind that your data is often already aggregated by your time series backend. Most time series queries do not return raw sample data, but instead include a group by time interval or maxDataPoints limit coupled with an aggregation function (usually average).",
      "headingPath": [
        "Introduction to histograms and heatmaps",
        "Raw data vs aggregated"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/fundamentals/intro-histograms/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "ae9ae70d7cf259aa312df4ed3911fb6863f59187",
        "sha256": "b6c9655954eab2f8d24641192907358c18408bfc0e465ac2466a617555ef6fee",
        "lineStart": 76,
        "lineEnd": 78,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/fundamentals/intro-histograms/index.md#L76-L78"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.d315e0c0960f2d7132e8",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "This all depends on the time range of your query of course. But the important point is to know that the histogram bucketing that Grafana performs might be done on already aggregated and averaged data. To get more accurate heatmaps, it is better to do the bucketing during metric collection, or to store the data in Elasticsearch or any other data source which supports doing histogram bucketing on the raw data.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Introduction to histograms and heatmaps",
        "Raw data vs aggregated"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/fundamentals/intro-histograms/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "ae9ae70d7cf259aa312df4ed3911fb6863f59187",
        "sha256": "b6c9655954eab2f8d24641192907358c18408bfc0e465ac2466a617555ef6fee",
        "lineStart": 80,
        "lineEnd": 83,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/fundamentals/intro-histograms/index.md#L80-L83"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.6f2b8fed19dc69035cb0",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "If you remove or lower the group by time (or raise maxDataPoints) in your query to return more data points, your heatmap will be more accurate, but this can also be very CPU and memory taxing for your browser, possibly causing hangs or crashes if the number of data points becomes unreasonably large.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Introduction to histograms and heatmaps",
        "Raw data vs aggregated"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/fundamentals/intro-histograms/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "ae9ae70d7cf259aa312df4ed3911fb6863f59187",
        "sha256": "b6c9655954eab2f8d24641192907358c18408bfc0e465ac2466a617555ef6fee",
        "lineStart": 85,
        "lineEnd": 87,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/fundamentals/intro-histograms/index.md#L85-L87"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.5b8b1d3813d128bb3954",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Observability focuses on understanding the internal state of your systems based on the data they produce, which helps determine if your infrastructure is healthy. Prometheus is a core technology for monitoring and observability of systems, but the term \"Prometheus\" can be confusing because it is used in different contexts. Understanding Prometheus basics, why it’s valuable for system observability, and how users use it in practice will both help you better understand it and help you use Grafana.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What is Prometheus?"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/fundamentals/intro-to-prometheus/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "67a7ad5bbbf0c122ceeaee29d5185df5a1d9b97a",
        "sha256": "424a69e21c2fd506098e6614598de989c1e2cc264ea18ef8a16b91556053f36e",
        "lineStart": 34,
        "lineEnd": 34,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/fundamentals/intro-to-prometheus/index.md#L34-L34"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.cd4041d658fad03dd0cd",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Prometheus began in 2012 at SoundCloud because existing technologies were insufficient for their observability needs. Prometheus offers both a robust data model and a query language. Prometheus is also simple and scalable. In 2018, Prometheus graduated from Cloud Native Computing Foundation (CNCF) incubation, and today has a thriving community.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What is Prometheus?"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/fundamentals/intro-to-prometheus/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "67a7ad5bbbf0c122ceeaee29d5185df5a1d9b97a",
        "sha256": "424a69e21c2fd506098e6614598de989c1e2cc264ea18ef8a16b91556053f36e",
        "lineStart": 36,
        "lineEnd": 36,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/fundamentals/intro-to-prometheus/index.md#L36-L36"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "mixed-edition-statement-requires-review",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.8c2818f5d84645097a66",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- _metrics_ that consist of a _timestamp_ and a _sample_, which is the numeric value, such as how many disk bytes have been read or a stock price",
      "headingPath": [
        "What is Prometheus?",
        "Prometheus as data"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/fundamentals/intro-to-prometheus/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "67a7ad5bbbf0c122ceeaee29d5185df5a1d9b97a",
        "sha256": "424a69e21c2fd506098e6614598de989c1e2cc264ea18ef8a16b91556053f36e",
        "lineStart": 48,
        "lineEnd": 48,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/fundamentals/intro-to-prometheus/index.md#L48-L48"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.9dc37220c0d020bb6211",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- a set of labels called _dimensions_, for example, `job` and `device`",
      "headingPath": [
        "What is Prometheus?",
        "Prometheus as data"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/fundamentals/intro-to-prometheus/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "67a7ad5bbbf0c122ceeaee29d5185df5a1d9b97a",
        "sha256": "424a69e21c2fd506098e6614598de989c1e2cc264ea18ef8a16b91556053f36e",
        "lineStart": 49,
        "lineEnd": 49,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/fundamentals/intro-to-prometheus/index.md#L49-L49"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.a0adbca602ba170f2cdd",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can store time series data in any relational database, however, these systems are not developed to store and query large volumes of time series data. Prometheus and similar software provide tools to compact and optimize time series data.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What is Prometheus?",
        "Prometheus as data"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/fundamentals/intro-to-prometheus/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "67a7ad5bbbf0c122ceeaee29d5185df5a1d9b97a",
        "sha256": "424a69e21c2fd506098e6614598de989c1e2cc264ea18ef8a16b91556053f36e",
        "lineStart": 51,
        "lineEnd": 51,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/fundamentals/intro-to-prometheus/index.md#L51-L51"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.6b268cf7791c43a9f7db",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The **Metrics browser** field contains the following query:",
      "headingPath": [
        "What is Prometheus?",
        "Prometheus as data",
        "Simple dashboard using PromQL"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/fundamentals/intro-to-prometheus/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "67a7ad5bbbf0c122ceeaee29d5185df5a1d9b97a",
        "sha256": "424a69e21c2fd506098e6614598de989c1e2cc264ea18ef8a16b91556053f36e",
        "lineStart": 57,
        "lineEnd": 57,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/fundamentals/intro-to-prometheus/index.md#L57-L57"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.d7ff837c8d500700076d",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The query is a simple example of [PromQL](/blog/2020/02/04/introduction-to-promql-the-prometheus-query-language/), the Prometheus Query Language. The query identifies the metric of interest (`node_disk_written_bytes_total`) and provides two labels (`job` and `device`). The label selector `job=\"integrations/macos-node\"` filters metrics. It both reduces the scope of the metrics to those coming from the MacOS integration job and specifies that the “device” label cannot be empty. The result of this query is the raw stream of numbers that the graph displays.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What is Prometheus?",
        "Prometheus as data",
        "Simple dashboard using PromQL"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/fundamentals/intro-to-prometheus/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "67a7ad5bbbf0c122ceeaee29d5185df5a1d9b97a",
        "sha256": "424a69e21c2fd506098e6614598de989c1e2cc264ea18ef8a16b91556053f36e",
        "lineStart": 65,
        "lineEnd": 65,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/fundamentals/intro-to-prometheus/index.md#L65-L65"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.62cdd74595d7c7400a34",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Although this view provides some insight into the performance of the system, it doesn’t provide the full story. A clearer picture of system performance requires understanding the rate of change that displays _how fast the data being written is changing_. To properly monitor disk performance, you need to also see spikes in activity that illustrate if and when the system is under load, and whether disk performance is at risk. PromQL includes a [rate()](https://prometheus.io/docs/prometheus/latest/querying/functions/#rate) function that shows the per-second average rate of increase over `5m` (5-minute) intervals. This view provides a much clearer picture of what’s happening with the system.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What is Prometheus?",
        "Prometheus as data",
        "Simple dashboard using PromQL"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/fundamentals/intro-to-prometheus/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "67a7ad5bbbf0c122ceeaee29d5185df5a1d9b97a",
        "sha256": "424a69e21c2fd506098e6614598de989c1e2cc264ea18ef8a16b91556053f36e",
        "lineStart": 67,
        "lineEnd": 67,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/fundamentals/intro-to-prometheus/index.md#L67-L67"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.dee30e5b1f7ad0b72d7c",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "A counter metric is just one type of metric; it is a number (such as total bytes written) that only increases. Prometheus [supports several others](https://prometheus.io/docs/concepts/metric_types/), such as the metric type `gauge`, which can increase or decrease.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What is Prometheus?",
        "Prometheus as data",
        "Simple dashboard using PromQL"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/fundamentals/intro-to-prometheus/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "67a7ad5bbbf0c122ceeaee29d5185df5a1d9b97a",
        "sha256": "424a69e21c2fd506098e6614598de989c1e2cc264ea18ef8a16b91556053f36e",
        "lineStart": 71,
        "lineEnd": 71,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/fundamentals/intro-to-prometheus/index.md#L71-L71"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.72e64c025800b8abf283",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The third metric type is called a `histogram`, which counts observations and organizes them into configurable groups. The following example displays floating-point numbers grouped into ranges that display how frequently each occurred.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What is Prometheus?",
        "Prometheus as data",
        "Simple dashboard using PromQL"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/fundamentals/intro-to-prometheus/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "67a7ad5bbbf0c122ceeaee29d5185df5a1d9b97a",
        "sha256": "424a69e21c2fd506098e6614598de989c1e2cc264ea18ef8a16b91556053f36e",
        "lineStart": 77,
        "lineEnd": 77,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/fundamentals/intro-to-prometheus/index.md#L77-L77"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.72607727195eef3b6016",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Software and systems are a difficult business. Sometimes things go wrong. Observability helps you understand a system’s state so that issues can be quickly identified and proactively addressed. And when problems do occur, you can be alerted to them to diagnose and solve them within your Service Level Objectives (SLOs).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What is Prometheus?",
        "Why this is valuable"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/fundamentals/intro-to-prometheus/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "67a7ad5bbbf0c122ceeaee29d5185df5a1d9b97a",
        "sha256": "424a69e21c2fd506098e6614598de989c1e2cc264ea18ef8a16b91556053f36e",
        "lineStart": 85,
        "lineEnd": 85,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/fundamentals/intro-to-prometheus/index.md#L85-L85"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.28a7d2176e0a12870877",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The [three pillars of observability](https://www.oreilly.com/library/view/distributed-systems-observability/9781492033431/ch04.html) are metrics, logs, and traces. Prometheus supports the metrics pillar. When software on a computer runs slowly, observability can help you identify whether CPU is saturated, the system is out of memory, or if the disk is writing at maximum speed so you can proactively respond.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What is Prometheus?",
        "Why this is valuable"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/fundamentals/intro-to-prometheus/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "67a7ad5bbbf0c122ceeaee29d5185df5a1d9b97a",
        "sha256": "424a69e21c2fd506098e6614598de989c1e2cc264ea18ef8a16b91556053f36e",
        "lineStart": 87,
        "lineEnd": 87,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/fundamentals/intro-to-prometheus/index.md#L87-L87"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.6139ad74f041565bf0eb",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Prometheus can scrape metric data from software and infrastructure and store it. Scraping means that Prometheus software periodically revisits the same endpoint to check for new data. Prometheus scrapes data from a piece of software instrumented with a client library.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What is Prometheus?",
        "Prometheus as software"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/fundamentals/intro-to-prometheus/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "67a7ad5bbbf0c122ceeaee29d5185df5a1d9b97a",
        "sha256": "424a69e21c2fd506098e6614598de989c1e2cc264ea18ef8a16b91556053f36e",
        "lineStart": 93,
        "lineEnd": 93,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/fundamentals/intro-to-prometheus/index.md#L93-L93"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.72d0ce555d9dc99caceb",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "For example, a NodeJS application can configure the [prom-client](https://github.com/siimon/prom-client) to expose metrics easily at an endpoint, and Prometheus can regularly scrape that endpoint. Prometheus includes a number of other tools within the toolkit to instrument your applications.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What is Prometheus?",
        "Prometheus as software"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/fundamentals/intro-to-prometheus/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "67a7ad5bbbf0c122ceeaee29d5185df5a1d9b97a",
        "sha256": "424a69e21c2fd506098e6614598de989c1e2cc264ea18ef8a16b91556053f36e",
        "lineStart": 95,
        "lineEnd": 95,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/fundamentals/intro-to-prometheus/index.md#L95-L95"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.4de3a2f9ac0f5af1f825",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Consider the following example. Suppose a 'MyApp' application uses a Prometheus client to expose metrics. One approach to collecting metrics data is to use a URL in the application that points to an endpoint `http://localhost:3000/metrics` that produces Prometheus metrics data.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What is Prometheus?",
        "Prometheus as deployment"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/fundamentals/intro-to-prometheus/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "67a7ad5bbbf0c122ceeaee29d5185df5a1d9b97a",
        "sha256": "424a69e21c2fd506098e6614598de989c1e2cc264ea18ef8a16b91556053f36e",
        "lineStart": 101,
        "lineEnd": 101,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/fundamentals/intro-to-prometheus/index.md#L101-L101"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.7c3e42e2554d0cca3e57",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The following image shows the two metrics associated with the endpoint. The HELP text explains what the metric means, and the TYPE text indicates what kind of metric it is (in this case, a gauge). `MyAppnodejs_active_request_total` indicates the number of requests (in this case, `1`). `MyAppnodejs_heap_size_total_bytes` indicates the heap size reported in bytes. There are only two numbers because this data shows the value at the moment the data was fetched.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What is Prometheus?",
        "Prometheus as deployment"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/fundamentals/intro-to-prometheus/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "67a7ad5bbbf0c122ceeaee29d5185df5a1d9b97a",
        "sha256": "424a69e21c2fd506098e6614598de989c1e2cc264ea18ef8a16b91556053f36e",
        "lineStart": 103,
        "lineEnd": 103,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/fundamentals/intro-to-prometheus/index.md#L103-L103"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.3d795ba61fee79136f1e",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "To get metrics into Grafana, you can use either the Prometheus software or [Grafana Alloy](https://grafana.com/docs/alloy/latest/) to scrape metrics. Grafana Alloy collects and forwards the telemetry data to open-source deployments of the Grafana Stack, Grafana Cloud, or Grafana Enterprise, where your data can be analyzed. For example, you can configure Grafana Alloy to pull the data from 'MyApp' every five seconds and send the results to Grafana Cloud.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What is Prometheus?",
        "Prometheus as deployment"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/fundamentals/intro-to-prometheus/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "67a7ad5bbbf0c122ceeaee29d5185df5a1d9b97a",
        "sha256": "424a69e21c2fd506098e6614598de989c1e2cc264ea18ef8a16b91556053f36e",
        "lineStart": 109,
        "lineEnd": 109,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/fundamentals/intro-to-prometheus/index.md#L109-L109"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "mixed-edition-statement-requires-review",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.b6a8467772463f6458d7",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Metrics data is only one type of telemetry data; the other kinds are logs and traces. Using Grafana Alloy can be a great option to send telemetry data because as you scale your observability practices to include logs and traces, which Grafana Alloy also supports, you've got a solution already in place.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What is Prometheus?",
        "Prometheus as deployment"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/fundamentals/intro-to-prometheus/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "67a7ad5bbbf0c122ceeaee29d5185df5a1d9b97a",
        "sha256": "424a69e21c2fd506098e6614598de989c1e2cc264ea18ef8a16b91556053f36e",
        "lineStart": 111,
        "lineEnd": 111,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/fundamentals/intro-to-prometheus/index.md#L111-L111"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.51883bcddf5313476d92",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The combination of Prometheus and Grafana Alloy gives you control over the metrics you want to report, where they come from, and where they’re going. Once the data is in Grafana, it can be stored in a Grafana Mimir database. Grafana dashboards consist of visualizations populated by data queried from the Prometheus data source. The PromQL query filters and aggregates the data to provide you the insight you need. With those steps, we’ve gone from raw numbers, generated by software, into Prometheus, delivered to Grafana, queried by PromQL, and visualized by Grafana.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What is Prometheus?",
        "Bringing it together"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/fundamentals/intro-to-prometheus/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "67a7ad5bbbf0c122ceeaee29d5185df5a1d9b97a",
        "sha256": "424a69e21c2fd506098e6614598de989c1e2cc264ea18ef8a16b91556053f36e",
        "lineStart": 119,
        "lineEnd": 119,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/fundamentals/intro-to-prometheus/index.md#L119-L119"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.04a88cc7b9e7fda12935",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- One great next step is to [build a dashboard](ref:build-dashboards) in Grafana and start turning that raw Prometheus telemetry data into insights about what’s going with your services and infrastructure.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What is Prometheus?",
        "What’s next?"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/fundamentals/intro-to-prometheus/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "67a7ad5bbbf0c122ceeaee29d5185df5a1d9b97a",
        "sha256": "424a69e21c2fd506098e6614598de989c1e2cc264ea18ef8a16b91556053f36e",
        "lineStart": 125,
        "lineEnd": 125,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/fundamentals/intro-to-prometheus/index.md#L125-L125"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.c74688cdc0f2d39c0ec9",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- Another great step is to learn about [Grafana Mimir](/oss/mimir/), which is essentially a database for Prometheus data. If you’re wondering how to make this work for a large volumes of metrics with a lot of data and fast querying, check out Grafana Mimir.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What is Prometheus?",
        "What’s next?"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/fundamentals/intro-to-prometheus/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "67a7ad5bbbf0c122ceeaee29d5185df5a1d9b97a",
        "sha256": "424a69e21c2fd506098e6614598de989c1e2cc264ea18ef8a16b91556053f36e",
        "lineStart": 126,
        "lineEnd": 126,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/fundamentals/intro-to-prometheus/index.md#L126-L126"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.d63c333c21374505216e",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- If you’re interested in working with Prometheus data in Grafana directly, check out the [Prometheus data source](ref:prometheus) documentation, or check out [PromQL basics](https://prometheus.io/docs/prometheus/latest/querying/basics/).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What is Prometheus?",
        "What’s next?"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/fundamentals/intro-to-prometheus/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "67a7ad5bbbf0c122ceeaee29d5185df5a1d9b97a",
        "sha256": "424a69e21c2fd506098e6614598de989c1e2cc264ea18ef8a16b91556053f36e",
        "lineStart": 127,
        "lineEnd": 127,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/fundamentals/intro-to-prometheus/index.md#L127-L127"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.b20ef7d008a8a9825c69",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "With time series data, the data often contain more than a single series, and is a set of multiple time series. Many Grafana data sources support this type of data.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Time series dimensions"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/fundamentals/timeseries-dimensions/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c02bffb45dbdb88a0f705767898428515302bfc8",
        "sha256": "852668c9e46b09bd4bba8390fada9d7a4e96bc0ceef6672ac022bf3ed05dc2a7",
        "lineStart": 41,
        "lineEnd": 41,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/fundamentals/timeseries-dimensions/index.md#L41-L41"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.0ff5b4cb3289c51d4f93",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The common case is issuing a single query for a measurement with one or more additional properties as dimensions. For example, querying a temperature measurement along with a location property. In this case, multiple series are returned back from that single query and each series has unique location as a dimension.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Time series dimensions"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/fundamentals/timeseries-dimensions/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c02bffb45dbdb88a0f705767898428515302bfc8",
        "sha256": "852668c9e46b09bd4bba8390fada9d7a4e96bc0ceef6672ac022bf3ed05dc2a7",
        "lineStart": 45,
        "lineEnd": 45,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/fundamentals/timeseries-dimensions/index.md#L45-L45"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.63dde4e0843246990cc7",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "To identify unique series within a set of time series, Grafana stores dimensions in _labels_.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Time series dimensions"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/fundamentals/timeseries-dimensions/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c02bffb45dbdb88a0f705767898428515302bfc8",
        "sha256": "852668c9e46b09bd4bba8390fada9d7a4e96bc0ceef6672ac022bf3ed05dc2a7",
        "lineStart": 47,
        "lineEnd": 47,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/fundamentals/timeseries-dimensions/index.md#L47-L47"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.7bec4220c51af2638c93",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Each time series in Grafana optionally has labels. Labels are a set of key/value pairs for identifying dimensions. Example labels could be `{location=us}` or `{country=us,state=ma,city=boston}`. Within a set of time series, the combination of its name and labels identifies each series. For example, `temperature {country=us,state=ma,city=boston}` could identify the series of temperature values for the city of Boston in the US.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Time series dimensions",
        "Labels"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/fundamentals/timeseries-dimensions/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c02bffb45dbdb88a0f705767898428515302bfc8",
        "sha256": "852668c9e46b09bd4bba8390fada9d7a4e96bc0ceef6672ac022bf3ed05dc2a7",
        "lineStart": 51,
        "lineEnd": 51,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/fundamentals/timeseries-dimensions/index.md#L51-L51"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.e4536f26472056137e7b",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Different sources of time series data have dimensions stored natively, or common storage patterns that allow the data to be extracted into dimensions.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Time series dimensions",
        "Labels"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/fundamentals/timeseries-dimensions/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c02bffb45dbdb88a0f705767898428515302bfc8",
        "sha256": "852668c9e46b09bd4bba8390fada9d7a4e96bc0ceef6672ac022bf3ed05dc2a7",
        "lineStart": 53,
        "lineEnd": 53,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/fundamentals/timeseries-dimensions/index.md#L53-L53"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.82cb41dc21915917ad09",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Time series databases (TSDBs) usually natively support dimensionality. Prometheus also stores dimensions in _labels_. In TSDBs such as Graphite or OpenTSDB the term _tags_ is used instead.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Time series dimensions",
        "Labels"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/fundamentals/timeseries-dimensions/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c02bffb45dbdb88a0f705767898428515302bfc8",
        "sha256": "852668c9e46b09bd4bba8390fada9d7a4e96bc0ceef6672ac022bf3ed05dc2a7",
        "lineStart": 55,
        "lineEnd": 55,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/fundamentals/timeseries-dimensions/index.md#L55-L55"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.8f798b201e19e7cfc2bf",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "In table databases such SQL, these dimensions are generally the `GROUP BY` parameters of a query.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Time series dimensions",
        "Labels"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/fundamentals/timeseries-dimensions/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c02bffb45dbdb88a0f705767898428515302bfc8",
        "sha256": "852668c9e46b09bd4bba8390fada9d7a4e96bc0ceef6672ac022bf3ed05dc2a7",
        "lineStart": 57,
        "lineEnd": 57,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/fundamentals/timeseries-dimensions/index.md#L57-L57"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.bb216267a6f6705dc8da",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "In SQL or SQL-like databases that return table responses, additional dimensions are usually represented as columns in the query response table.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Time series dimensions",
        "Multiple dimensions in table format"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/fundamentals/timeseries-dimensions/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c02bffb45dbdb88a0f705767898428515302bfc8",
        "sha256": "852668c9e46b09bd4bba8390fada9d7a4e96bc0ceef6672ac022bf3ed05dc2a7",
        "lineStart": 61,
        "lineEnd": 61,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/fundamentals/timeseries-dimensions/index.md#L61-L61"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.b782411707c3800838a2",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "For example, consider a query like:",
      "headingPath": [
        "Time series dimensions",
        "Multiple dimensions in table format",
        "Single dimension"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/fundamentals/timeseries-dimensions/index.md",
