    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.64999ff19cd4d2f0c903",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "More than one dimension is currently only supported in the Logs queries within the Azure Monitor service as of version 7.1.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Time series dimensions",
        "Multiple dimensions in table format",
        "Multiple dimensions"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/fundamentals/timeseries-dimensions/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c02bffb45dbdb88a0f705767898428515302bfc8",
        "sha256": "852668c9e46b09bd4bba8390fada9d7a4e96bc0ceef6672ac022bf3ed05dc2a7",
        "lineStart": 104,
        "lineEnd": 104,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/fundamentals/timeseries-dimensions/index.md#L104-L104"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.c0a827b3d8e1895e03c9",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Multiple dimensions are not supported in a way that maps to multiple alerts in Grafana, but rather they are treated as multiple conditions to a single alert. For more information, see the documentation on [creating alerts with multiple series](ref:create-grafana-managed-rule).",
      "headingPath": [
        "Time series dimensions",
        "Multiple dimensions in table format",
        "Multiple dimensions"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/fundamentals/timeseries-dimensions/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c02bffb45dbdb88a0f705767898428515302bfc8",
        "sha256": "852668c9e46b09bd4bba8390fada9d7a4e96bc0ceef6672ac022bf3ed05dc2a7",
        "lineStart": 108,
        "lineEnd": 109,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/fundamentals/timeseries-dimensions/index.md#L108-L109"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.0c06a8dbe7b4dd09bad4",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "In the case of SQL-like data sources, more than one numeric column can be selected, with or without additional string columns to be used as dimensions. For example, `AVG(Temperature) AS AvgTemp, MAX(Temperature) AS MaxTemp`. This, if combined with multiple dimensions, can result in a lot of series. Selecting multiple values is currently only designed to be used with visualization.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Time series dimensions",
        "Multiple dimensions in table format",
        "Multiple values"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/fundamentals/timeseries-dimensions/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c02bffb45dbdb88a0f705767898428515302bfc8",
        "sha256": "852668c9e46b09bd4bba8390fada9d7a4e96bc0ceef6672ac022bf3ed05dc2a7",
        "lineStart": 114,
        "lineEnd": 114,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/fundamentals/timeseries-dimensions/index.md#L114-L114"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.795ebb2f14a810a95c13",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Additional technical information on tabular time series formats and how dimensions are extracted can be found in [the developer documentation on data frames as time series](https://grafana.com/developers/plugin-tools/key-concepts/data-frames#data-frames-as-time-series).",
      "headingPath": [
        "Time series dimensions",
        "Multiple dimensions in table format",
        "Multiple values"
      ],
