    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.a16984cc5166f4a2c000",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- New data is appended at the end, at regular intervals — for example, hourly at 09:00, 10:00, 11:00, and so on.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Introduction to time series"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/fundamentals/timeseries/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "aaa0df85d3c9a6ee56133f232af61ea75f549ce0",
        "sha256": "91cb08c8677efd98f7a5d0d1853fc98b712f1ea37e4e5dec5fb499108e697400",
        "lineStart": 45,
        "lineEnd": 45,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/fundamentals/timeseries/index.md#L45-L45"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.7431aa09fffba860ebc0",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- Measurements are seldom updated after they were added — for example, yesterday's temperature doesn't change.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Introduction to time series"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/fundamentals/timeseries/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "aaa0df85d3c9a6ee56133f232af61ea75f549ce0",
        "sha256": "91cb08c8677efd98f7a5d0d1853fc98b712f1ea37e4e5dec5fb499108e697400",
        "lineStart": 46,
        "lineEnd": 46,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/fundamentals/timeseries/index.md#L46-L46"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.c14cd2d69809966616f2",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Time series can also help you predict the future, by uncovering trends in your data. If the number of registered users has been increasing monthly by 4% for the past few months, you can predict how big your user base is going to be at the end of the year.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Introduction to time series"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/fundamentals/timeseries/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "aaa0df85d3c9a6ee56133f232af61ea75f549ce0",
        "sha256": "91cb08c8677efd98f7a5d0d1853fc98b712f1ea37e4e5dec5fb499108e697400",
        "lineStart": 50,
        "lineEnd": 50,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/fundamentals/timeseries/index.md#L50-L50"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.f57d9b9115e6a289cbaf",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Some time series have patterns that repeat themselves over a known period. For example, the temperature is typically higher during the day, before it dips down at night. By identifying these periodic, or _seasonal_, time series, you can make confident predictions about the next period. If you know that the system load peaks every day around 18:00, you can add more machines right before.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Introduction to time series"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/fundamentals/timeseries/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "aaa0df85d3c9a6ee56133f232af61ea75f549ce0",
        "sha256": "91cb08c8677efd98f7a5d0d1853fc98b712f1ea37e4e5dec5fb499108e697400",
        "lineStart": 52,
        "lineEnd": 52,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/fundamentals/timeseries/index.md#L52-L52"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.ed096d85c8f310729a95",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Depending on what you're measuring, the data can vary greatly. What if you wanted to compare periods longer than the interval between measurements? If you'd measure the temperature once every hour, you'd end up with 24 data points per day. To compare the temperature in August over the years, you'd have to combine the 31 times 24 data points into one.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Introduction to time series",
        "Aggregating time series"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/fundamentals/timeseries/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "aaa0df85d3c9a6ee56133f232af61ea75f549ce0",
        "sha256": "91cb08c8677efd98f7a5d0d1853fc98b712f1ea37e4e5dec5fb499108e697400",
        "lineStart": 56,
        "lineEnd": 56,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/fundamentals/timeseries/index.md#L56-L56"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.788e8b113e8202435488",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- **Average** returns the sum of all values divided by the total number of values.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Introduction to time series",
        "Aggregating time series"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/fundamentals/timeseries/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "aaa0df85d3c9a6ee56133f232af61ea75f549ce0",
        "sha256": "91cb08c8677efd98f7a5d0d1853fc98b712f1ea37e4e5dec5fb499108e697400",
        "lineStart": 60,
        "lineEnd": 60,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/fundamentals/timeseries/index.md#L60-L60"
      },
      "applicability": {
