    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.0fa5915e280fda7577ec",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Modern time series databases take advantage of the fact that measurements are only ever appended, and rarely updated or removed. For example, the timestamps for each measurement change very little over time, which results in redundant data being stored.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Introduction to time series",
        "Time series and monitoring",
        "Time series databases"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/fundamentals/timeseries/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "aaa0df85d3c9a6ee56133f232af61ea75f549ce0",
        "sha256": "91cb08c8677efd98f7a5d0d1853fc98b712f1ea37e4e5dec5fb499108e697400",
        "lineStart": 77,
        "lineEnd": 77,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/fundamentals/timeseries/index.md#L77-L77"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.b84de8a1f615ae776ae2",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Looking at these timestamps, they all start with `1572524`, leading to poor use of disk space. Instead, we could store each subsequent timestamp as the difference, or _delta_, from the first one:",
      "headingPath": [
        "Introduction to time series",
        "Time series and monitoring",
        "Time series databases"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/fundamentals/timeseries/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "aaa0df85d3c9a6ee56133f232af61ea75f549ce0",
        "sha256": "91cb08c8677efd98f7a5d0d1853fc98b712f1ea37e4e5dec5fb499108e697400",
        "lineStart": 85,
        "lineEnd": 85,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/fundamentals/timeseries/index.md#L85-L85"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.91ce918756d370e14a0b",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "If measurements are taken at regular intervals, most of these delta-of-deltas will be 0. Because of optimizations like these, TSDBs use drastically less space than other databases.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Introduction to time series",
        "Time series and monitoring",
        "Time series databases"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/fundamentals/timeseries/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "aaa0df85d3c9a6ee56133f232af61ea75f549ce0",
        "sha256": "91cb08c8677efd98f7a5d0d1853fc98b712f1ea37e4e5dec5fb499108e697400",
        "lineStart": 97,
        "lineEnd": 97,
