    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.ff770d49c9d72959974d",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "If you're using Grafana Alerting, then you can have alerts sent through a number of different alert notifiers, including PagerDuty, SMS, email, VictorOps, OpsGenie, or Slack.",
      "headingPath": [
        "About Grafana",
        "Alerts"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/introduction/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "d35a49c57b8a1382110f2440c733dd8414763c6d",
        "sha256": "4440c9df85f387c01946f1c1d22f986808a46ee19a31b5c631d9fb33a915c428",
        "lineStart": 29,
        "lineEnd": 29,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/introduction/_index.md#L29-L29"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.9e409e6cbc6bd242e333",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Alert hooks allow you to create different notifiers with a bit of code if you prefer some other channels of communication. Visually define [alert rules](../alerting/alerting-rules/) for your most important metrics.",
      "headingPath": [
        "About Grafana",
        "Alerts"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/introduction/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "d35a49c57b8a1382110f2440c733dd8414763c6d",
        "sha256": "4440c9df85f387c01946f1c1d22f986808a46ee19a31b5c631d9fb33a915c428",
        "lineStart": 31,
        "lineEnd": 31,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/introduction/_index.md#L31-L31"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.1b42ab5a2709370e4bc9",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "This feature, which shows up as a graph marker in Grafana, is useful for correlating data in case something goes wrong. You can create the annotations manually—just control-click on a graph and input some text—or you can fetch data from any data source. Refer to [Annotations](../dashboards/build-dashboards/annotate-visualizations/) for more information.",
      "headingPath": [
        "About Grafana",
        "Annotations"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/introduction/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "d35a49c57b8a1382110f2440c733dd8414763c6d",
        "sha256": "4440c9df85f387c01946f1c1d22f986808a46ee19a31b5c631d9fb33a915c428",
        "lineStart": 37,
        "lineEnd": 37,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/introduction/_index.md#L37-L37"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.9fc2f76d4472aa61a35c",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "[Template variables](../dashboards/variables/) allow you to create dashboards that can be reused for lots of different use cases. Values aren't hard-coded with these templates, so for instance, if you have a production server and a test server, you can use the same dashboard for both.",
      "headingPath": [
        "About Grafana",
        "Dashboard variables"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/introduction/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "d35a49c57b8a1382110f2440c733dd8414763c6d",
        "sha256": "4440c9df85f387c01946f1c1d22f986808a46ee19a31b5c631d9fb33a915c428",
        "lineStart": 45,
        "lineEnd": 45,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/introduction/_index.md#L45-L45"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.52bc5d0ad33a6c9f09f0",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Templating allows you to drill down into your data, say, from all data to North America data, down to Texas data, and beyond. You can also share these dashboards across teams within your organization—or if you create a great dashboard template for a popular data source, you can contribute it to the whole community to customize and use.",
      "headingPath": [
        "About Grafana",
        "Dashboard variables"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/introduction/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "d35a49c57b8a1382110f2440c733dd8414763c6d",
        "sha256": "4440c9df85f387c01946f1c1d22f986808a46ee19a31b5c631d9fb33a915c428",
        "lineStart": 47,
        "lineEnd": 47,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/introduction/_index.md#L47-L47"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.626a53b5d3d85b680475",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "If you're a Grafana administrator, then you'll want to thoroughly familiarize yourself with [Grafana configuration options](../setup-grafana/configure-grafana/) and the [Grafana CLI](../cli/).",
      "headingPath": [
        "About Grafana",
        "Configure Grafana"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/introduction/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "d35a49c57b8a1382110f2440c733dd8414763c6d",
        "sha256": "4440c9df85f387c01946f1c1d22f986808a46ee19a31b5c631d9fb33a915c428",
        "lineStart": 51,
        "lineEnd": 51,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/introduction/_index.md#L51-L51"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.c6316f4e1190c36ad94b",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Configuration covers both config files and environment variables. You can set up default ports, logging levels, email IP addresses, security, and more.",
      "headingPath": [
        "About Grafana",
        "Configure Grafana"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/introduction/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "d35a49c57b8a1382110f2440c733dd8414763c6d",
        "sha256": "4440c9df85f387c01946f1c1d22f986808a46ee19a31b5c631d9fb33a915c428",
        "lineStart": 53,
        "lineEnd": 53,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/introduction/_index.md#L53-L53"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.6620f119b1c1bb428c52",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "While it's easy to click, drag, and drop to create a single dashboard, power users in need of many dashboards will want to automate the setup with a script. You can script anything in Grafana.",
      "headingPath": [
        "About Grafana",
        "Provisioning"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/introduction/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "d35a49c57b8a1382110f2440c733dd8414763c6d",
        "sha256": "4440c9df85f387c01946f1c1d22f986808a46ee19a31b5c631d9fb33a915c428",
        "lineStart": 57,
        "lineEnd": 57,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/introduction/_index.md#L57-L57"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.7890feb171da03ea2e5d",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "For example, if you're spinning up a new Kubernetes cluster, you can also spin up a Grafana automatically with a script that would have the right server, IP address, and data sources preset and locked in so users cannot change them. It's also a way of getting control over a lot of dashboards. Refer to [Provisioning](../administration/provisioning/) for more information.",
      "headingPath": [
        "About Grafana",
        "Provisioning"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/introduction/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "d35a49c57b8a1382110f2440c733dd8414763c6d",
        "sha256": "4440c9df85f387c01946f1c1d22f986808a46ee19a31b5c631d9fb33a915c428",
        "lineStart": 59,
        "lineEnd": 59,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/introduction/_index.md#L59-L59"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.02a30d21620f404988e6",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Grafana supports different authentication methods, such as LDAP and OAuth, and allows you to map users to organizations. Refer to the [User authentication overview](../setup-grafana/configure-access/configure-authentication/) for more information.",
      "headingPath": [
        "About Grafana",
        "Authentication"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/introduction/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "d35a49c57b8a1382110f2440c733dd8414763c6d",
        "sha256": "4440c9df85f387c01946f1c1d22f986808a46ee19a31b5c631d9fb33a915c428",
        "lineStart": 63,
        "lineEnd": 63,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/introduction/_index.md#L63-L63"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.72e4c77cc82291189321",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "In Grafana Enterprise, you can also map users to teams: If your company has its own authentication system, Grafana allows you to map the teams in your internal systems to teams in Grafana. That way, you can automatically give people access to the dashboards designated for their teams. Refer to [Grafana Enterprise](grafana-enterprise/) for more information.",
      "headingPath": [
        "About Grafana",
        "Authentication"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/introduction/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "d35a49c57b8a1382110f2440c733dd8414763c6d",
        "sha256": "4440c9df85f387c01946f1c1d22f986808a46ee19a31b5c631d9fb33a915c428",
        "lineStart": 65,
        "lineEnd": 65,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/introduction/_index.md#L65-L65"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "mixed-edition-statement-requires-review",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.af5ea0ebe3f09621e9a1",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "When organizations have one Grafana and multiple teams, they often want the ability to both keep things separate and share dashboards. You can create a team of users and then set permissions on [folders and dashboards](../administration/user-management/manage-dashboard-permissions/), and down to the [data source level](../administration/data-source-management/#data-source-permissions) if you're using [Grafana Enterprise](grafana-enterprise/).",
      "headingPath": [
        "About Grafana",
        "Permissions"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/introduction/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "d35a49c57b8a1382110f2440c733dd8414763c6d",
        "sha256": "4440c9df85f387c01946f1c1d22f986808a46ee19a31b5c631d9fb33a915c428",
        "lineStart": 69,
        "lineEnd": 69,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/introduction/_index.md#L69-L69"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "mixed-edition-statement-requires-review",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.7fc2ca9d1675593c05cf",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "In addition to Grafana, Grafana Labs also provides the following open source projects:",
      "headingPath": [
        "About Grafana",
        "Other Grafana Labs OSS Projects"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/introduction/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "d35a49c57b8a1382110f2440c733dd8414763c6d",
        "sha256": "4440c9df85f387c01946f1c1d22f986808a46ee19a31b5c631d9fb33a915c428",
        "lineStart": 73,
        "lineEnd": 73,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/introduction/_index.md#L73-L73"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.3a407a30baeab6ad3ec3",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "**Grafana Loki:** Grafana Loki is an open source, set of components that can be composed into a fully featured logging stack. For more information, refer to [Grafana Loki documentation](/docs/loki/latest/).",
      "headingPath": [
        "About Grafana",
        "Other Grafana Labs OSS Projects"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/introduction/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "d35a49c57b8a1382110f2440c733dd8414763c6d",
        "sha256": "4440c9df85f387c01946f1c1d22f986808a46ee19a31b5c631d9fb33a915c428",
        "lineStart": 75,
        "lineEnd": 75,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/introduction/_index.md#L75-L75"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.20d2ed93722170471588",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "**Grafana Tempo:** Grafana Tempo is an open source, easy-to-use and high-volume distributed tracing backend. For more information, refer to [Grafana Tempo documentation](/docs/tempo/latest/?pg=oss-tempo&plcmt=hero-txt/).",
      "headingPath": [
        "About Grafana",
        "Other Grafana Labs OSS Projects"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/introduction/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "d35a49c57b8a1382110f2440c733dd8414763c6d",
        "sha256": "4440c9df85f387c01946f1c1d22f986808a46ee19a31b5c631d9fb33a915c428",
        "lineStart": 77,
        "lineEnd": 77,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/introduction/_index.md#L77-L77"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.47817c95d9e845cfc430",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "**Grafana Mimir:** Grafana Mimir is an open source software project that provides a scalable long-term storage for Prometheus. For more information about Grafana Mimir, refer to [Grafana Mimir documentation](/docs/mimir/latest/).",
      "headingPath": [
        "About Grafana",
        "Other Grafana Labs OSS Projects"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/introduction/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "d35a49c57b8a1382110f2440c733dd8414763c6d",
        "sha256": "4440c9df85f387c01946f1c1d22f986808a46ee19a31b5c631d9fb33a915c428",
        "lineStart": 79,
        "lineEnd": 79,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/introduction/_index.md#L79-L79"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.15b4f7edbcb1e0a2820b",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "**Grafana Pyroscope:** Grafana Pyroscope is an open source software project for aggregating continuous profiling data. Continuous profiling is an observability signal that allows you to understand your workload's resources (CPU, memory, for example) usage down to the line number. For more information about Grafana Pyroscope, refer to [Grafana Pyroscope documentation](/docs/pyroscope/latest/).",
      "headingPath": [
        "About Grafana",
        "Other Grafana Labs OSS Projects"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/introduction/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "d35a49c57b8a1382110f2440c733dd8414763c6d",
        "sha256": "4440c9df85f387c01946f1c1d22f986808a46ee19a31b5c631d9fb33a915c428",
        "lineStart": 81,
        "lineEnd": 81,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/introduction/_index.md#L81-L81"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.05fa1997c083692c0921",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "**Grafana Beyla:** Grafana Beyla is an eBPF-based application auto-instrumentation tool for application observability. eBPF is used to automatically inspect application executables and the OS networking layer as well as capture basic trace spans related to web transactions and Rate-Errors-Duration (RED) metrics for Linux HTTP/S and gRPC services. All data capture occurs without any modifications to application code or configuration. For more information about Grafana Beyla, refer to [Grafana Beyla documentation](/docs/beyla/latest/).",
      "headingPath": [
        "About Grafana",
        "Other Grafana Labs OSS Projects"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/introduction/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "d35a49c57b8a1382110f2440c733dd8414763c6d",
        "sha256": "4440c9df85f387c01946f1c1d22f986808a46ee19a31b5c631d9fb33a915c428",
        "lineStart": 85,
        "lineEnd": 85,
