    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.129fd75e849a6e189eb3",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can assign roles through the user interface or APIs, establish them through Terraform, or synchronize them automatically via an external IAM provider.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Plan your IAM integration strategy",
        "How to work with roles?"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-access/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "63f14286dc00550c860501a81f311188c9f26bde",
        "sha256": "b225f8d5068b6e330e18c0916c7295be963d055af907c0790708a7bbd383b7af",
        "lineStart": 143,
        "lineEnd": 143,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-access/_index.md#L143-L143"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "unresolved-no-explicit-oss-products-label",
        "products": []
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.a5e780890b8b403ccd69",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Within an organization, Grafana has established three primary [organization roles](../../administration/roles-and-permissions/#organization-roles) - organization administrator, editor, and viewer - which dictate the user's level of access and permissions, including the ability to edit data sources or create teams. Grafana also has an empty role that you can start with and to which you can gradually add custom permissions. To be a member of any organization, every user must be assigned a role.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Plan your IAM integration strategy",
        "How to work with roles?",
        "What are roles?"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-access/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "63f14286dc00550c860501a81f311188c9f26bde",
        "sha256": "b225f8d5068b6e330e18c0916c7295be963d055af907c0790708a7bbd383b7af",
        "lineStart": 147,
        "lineEnd": 148,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-access/_index.md#L147-L148"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "unresolved-no-explicit-oss-products-label",
        "products": []
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.dbd70aa442f173169dba",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "In addition, Grafana provides a server administrator role that grants access to and enables interaction with resources that affect the entire instance, including organizations, users, and server-wide settings. This particular role can only be accessed by users of self-hosted Grafana instances. It is a significant role intended for the administrators of the Grafana instance.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Plan your IAM integration strategy",
        "How to work with roles?",
        "What are roles?"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-access/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "63f14286dc00550c860501a81f311188c9f26bde",
        "sha256": "b225f8d5068b6e330e18c0916c7295be963d055af907c0790708a7bbd383b7af",
        "lineStart": 150,
        "lineEnd": 151,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-access/_index.md#L150-L151"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "unresolved-no-explicit-oss-products-label",
        "products": []
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.cc79382fbb69ce7f35c1",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Each role consists of a set of [permissions](../../administration/roles-and-permissions/#dashboard-permissions) that determine the tasks a user can perform in the system. For example, the **Admin** role includes permissions that let an administrator create and delete users.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Plan your IAM integration strategy",
        "How to work with roles?",
        "What are permissions?"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-access/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "63f14286dc00550c860501a81f311188c9f26bde",
        "sha256": "b225f8d5068b6e330e18c0916c7295be963d055af907c0790708a7bbd383b7af",
        "lineStart": 155,
        "lineEnd": 156,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-access/_index.md#L155-L156"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "unresolved-no-explicit-oss-products-label",
        "products": []
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.9dab9ef1fccec64b76a8",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Grafana allows for precise permission settings on both dashboards and folders, giving you the ability to control which users and teams can view, edit, and administer them. For example, you might want a certain viewer to be able to edit a dashboard. While that user can see all dashboards, you can grant them access to update only one of them.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Plan your IAM integration strategy",
        "How to work with roles?",
        "What are permissions?"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-access/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "63f14286dc00550c860501a81f311188c9f26bde",
        "sha256": "b225f8d5068b6e330e18c0916c7295be963d055af907c0790708a7bbd383b7af",
        "lineStart": 158,
        "lineEnd": 159,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-access/_index.md#L158-L159"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "unresolved-no-explicit-oss-products-label",
        "products": []
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.3f9c57b4724b029680d2",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "In [Grafana Enterprise](../../introduction/grafana-enterprise/), you can also grant granular permissions for data sources to control who can query and edit them.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Plan your IAM integration strategy",
        "How to work with roles?",
        "What are permissions?"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-access/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "63f14286dc00550c860501a81f311188c9f26bde",
        "sha256": "b225f8d5068b6e330e18c0916c7295be963d055af907c0790708a7bbd383b7af",
        "lineStart": 161,
        "lineEnd": 161,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-access/_index.md#L161-L161"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "mixed-edition-statement-requires-review",
        "products": []
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.e7b9d9eab897682899ec",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Dashboard, folder, and data source permissions can be set through the UI or APIs or provisioned through Terraform.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Plan your IAM integration strategy",
        "How to work with roles?",
        "What are permissions?"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-access/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "63f14286dc00550c860501a81f311188c9f26bde",
        "sha256": "b225f8d5068b6e330e18c0916c7295be963d055af907c0790708a7bbd383b7af",
        "lineStart": 163,
        "lineEnd": 163,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-access/_index.md#L163-L163"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "unresolved-no-explicit-oss-products-label",
        "products": []
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.263ba44e95f8889f446c",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "If you think that the basic organization and server administrator roles are too limiting, it might be beneficial to employ [role-based access control (RBAC)](../../administration/roles-and-permissions/access-control/). RBAC is a flexible approach to managing user access to Grafana resources, including users, data sources, and reports. It enables easy granting, changing, and revoking of read and write access for users.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Plan your IAM integration strategy",
        "How to work with roles?",
        "Role-based access control"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-access/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "63f14286dc00550c860501a81f311188c9f26bde",
        "sha256": "b225f8d5068b6e330e18c0916c7295be963d055af907c0790708a7bbd383b7af",
        "lineStart": 171,
        "lineEnd": 172,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-access/_index.md#L171-L172"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "unresolved-no-explicit-oss-products-label",
        "products": []
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.f3565004c1687b9922ae",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "RBAC comes with pre-defined roles, such as data source writer, which allows updating, reading, or querying all data sources. You can assign these roles to users, teams, and service accounts.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Plan your IAM integration strategy",
        "How to work with roles?",
        "Role-based access control"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-access/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "63f14286dc00550c860501a81f311188c9f26bde",
        "sha256": "b225f8d5068b6e330e18c0916c7295be963d055af907c0790708a7bbd383b7af",
        "lineStart": 174,
        "lineEnd": 175,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-access/_index.md#L174-L175"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "unresolved-no-explicit-oss-products-label",
        "products": []
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.e80a3b93e037bd77a0e3",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "When connecting Grafana to an identity provider, it's important to think beyond just the initial authentication setup. You should also think about the maintenance of user bases and roles. Using Grafana's team and role synchronization features ensures that updates you make to a user in your identity provider will be reflected in their role assignment and team memberships in Grafana.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Plan your IAM integration strategy",
        "User synchronization between Grafana and identity providers"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-access/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "63f14286dc00550c860501a81f311188c9f26bde",
        "sha256": "b225f8d5068b6e330e18c0916c7295be963d055af907c0790708a7bbd383b7af",
        "lineStart": 181,
        "lineEnd": 181,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-access/_index.md#L181-L181"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "unresolved-no-explicit-oss-products-label",
        "products": []
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.9f4f9018595ccfe58e9b",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Team sync is a feature that allows you to synchronize teams or groups from your authentication provider with teams in Grafana. This means that users of specific teams or groups in LDAP, OAuth, or SAML will be automatically added or removed as members of corresponding teams in Grafana. Whenever a user logs in, Grafana will check for any changes in the teams or groups of the authentication provider and update the user's teams in Grafana accordingly. This makes it easy to manage user permissions across multiple systems.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Plan your IAM integration strategy",
        "User synchronization between Grafana and identity providers",
        "Team sync"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-access/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "63f14286dc00550c860501a81f311188c9f26bde",
        "sha256": "b225f8d5068b6e330e18c0916c7295be963d055af907c0790708a7bbd383b7af",
        "lineStart": 185,
        "lineEnd": 185,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-access/_index.md#L185-L185"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "unresolved-no-explicit-oss-products-label",
        "products": []
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.9fff4dc3521cccb542ad",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Available in [Grafana Enterprise](../../introduction/grafana-enterprise/) and to customers on select Grafana Cloud plans. For pricing information, visit [pricing](https://grafana.com/pricing/) or contact our sales team.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Plan your IAM integration strategy",
        "User synchronization between Grafana and identity providers",
        "Team sync"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-access/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "63f14286dc00550c860501a81f311188c9f26bde",
        "sha256": "b225f8d5068b6e330e18c0916c7295be963d055af907c0790708a7bbd383b7af",
        "lineStart": 188,
        "lineEnd": 188,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-access/_index.md#L188-L188"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "mixed-edition-statement-requires-review",
        "products": []
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.f61064ccd15c8074e15c",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Team synchronization occurs only when a user logs in. However, if you are using LDAP, it is possible to enable active background synchronization. This allows for the continuous synchronization of teams.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Plan your IAM integration strategy",
        "User synchronization between Grafana and identity providers",
        "Team sync"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-access/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "63f14286dc00550c860501a81f311188c9f26bde",
        "sha256": "b225f8d5068b6e330e18c0916c7295be963d055af907c0790708a7bbd383b7af",
        "lineStart": 192,
        "lineEnd": 192,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-access/_index.md#L192-L192"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "unresolved-no-explicit-oss-products-label",
        "products": []
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.f84c3a6b939c98b7518e",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Grafana can synchronize basic roles from your authentication provider by mapping attributes from the identity provider to the user role in Grafana. This means that users with specific attributes, like role, team, or group membership in LDAP, OAuth, or SAML, can be automatically assigned the corresponding role in Grafana. Whenever a user logs in, Grafana checks for any changes in the user information retrieved from the authentication provider and updates the user's role in Grafana accordingly.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Plan your IAM integration strategy",
        "User synchronization between Grafana and identity providers",
        "Role Sync"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-access/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "63f14286dc00550c860501a81f311188c9f26bde",
        "sha256": "b225f8d5068b6e330e18c0916c7295be963d055af907c0790708a7bbd383b7af",
        "lineStart": 197,
        "lineEnd": 197,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-access/_index.md#L197-L197"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "unresolved-no-explicit-oss-products-label",
        "products": []
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.0c720b1fd0e31d62f7de",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "With organization sync, you can assign users from identity provider groups to corresponding Grafana organizations. This functionality is similar to role sync but with the added benefit of specifying the organization that a user belongs to for a particular identity provider group. Please note that this feature is only available for self-hosted Grafana instances, as Cloud Grafana instances have a single organization limit.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Plan your IAM integration strategy",
        "User synchronization between Grafana and identity providers",
        "Organization sync"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-access/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "63f14286dc00550c860501a81f311188c9f26bde",
        "sha256": "b225f8d5068b6e330e18c0916c7295be963d055af907c0790708a7bbd383b7af",
        "lineStart": 203,
        "lineEnd": 203,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-access/_index.md#L203-L203"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "conditional-or-paid-restriction-requires-review",
        "products": []
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.fb90194ee1ff40f79acb",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- Organization sync is currently only supported for SAML and LDAP.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Plan your IAM integration strategy",
        "User synchronization between Grafana and identity providers",
        "Organization sync"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-access/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "63f14286dc00550c860501a81f311188c9f26bde",
        "sha256": "b225f8d5068b6e330e18c0916c7295be963d055af907c0790708a7bbd383b7af",
        "lineStart": 209,
        "lineEnd": 209,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-access/_index.md#L209-L209"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "unresolved-no-explicit-oss-products-label",
        "products": []
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.0d6e58d44daf6c51498e",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- You can only map basic roles with Organization sync.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Plan your IAM integration strategy",
        "User synchronization between Grafana and identity providers",
        "Organization sync"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-access/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "63f14286dc00550c860501a81f311188c9f26bde",
        "sha256": "b225f8d5068b6e330e18c0916c7295be963d055af907c0790708a7bbd383b7af",
        "lineStart": 210,
        "lineEnd": 210,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-access/_index.md#L210-L210"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "unresolved-no-explicit-oss-products-label",
        "products": []
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.1460d583b78fff5a325e",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- You don't need to invite users through Grafana when syncing with Organization sync.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Plan your IAM integration strategy",
        "User synchronization between Grafana and identity providers",
        "Organization sync"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-access/_index.md",
