    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.013b88997eafa3897316",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can configure Grafana to let a HTTP reverse proxy handle authentication. Popular web servers have a very extensive list of pluggable authentication modules, and any of them can be used with the AuthProxy feature. Below we detail the configuration options for auth proxy.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Configure auth proxy authentication"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-access/configure-authentication/auth-proxy/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "9a79b026fbdf94cc528ae47537d1a00d347ad48a",
        "sha256": "fa803a39ed5121a5bc3cd9e90c23855d067d46c7e0ef1fa5d076af5a7b13ba7d",
        "lineStart": 25,
        "lineEnd": 27,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-access/configure-authentication/auth-proxy/index.md#L25-L27"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.340abb48191ef57b4bfa",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "We can then send a second request to the `/api/user` method which will return the details of the logged in user. We will use this request to show how Grafana automatically adds the new user we specify to the system. Here we create a new user called “anthony”.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Configure auth proxy authentication",
        "Interacting with Grafana’s AuthProxy via curl"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-access/configure-authentication/auth-proxy/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "9a79b026fbdf94cc528ae47537d1a00d347ad48a",
        "sha256": "fa803a39ed5121a5bc3cd9e90c23855d067d46c7e0ef1fa5d076af5a7b13ba7d",
        "lineStart": 71,
        "lineEnd": 71,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-access/configure-authentication/auth-proxy/index.md#L71-L71"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.3a509d85b6c44dc8472f",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "I’ll demonstrate how to use Apache for authenticating users. In this example we use BasicAuth with Apache’s text file based authentication handler, i.e. htpasswd files. However, any available Apache authentication capabilities could be used.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Configure auth proxy authentication",
        "Making Apache’s auth work together with Grafana’s AuthProxy"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-access/configure-authentication/auth-proxy/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "9a79b026fbdf94cc528ae47537d1a00d347ad48a",
        "sha256": "fa803a39ed5121a5bc3cd9e90c23855d067d46c7e0ef1fa5d076af5a7b13ba7d",
        "lineStart": 87,
        "lineEnd": 87,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-access/configure-authentication/auth-proxy/index.md#L87-L87"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.08cddb1da3d65df2ec50",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "In this example we use Apache as a reverse proxy in front of Grafana. Apache handles the Authentication of users before forwarding requests to the Grafana backend service.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Configure auth proxy authentication",
        "Making Apache’s auth work together with Grafana’s AuthProxy",
        "Apache BasicAuth"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-access/configure-authentication/auth-proxy/index.md",
