    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.eefdba61f56eaf86d46e",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- Launch the Apache HTTP server container using our custom `httpd.conf` and our `htpasswd` file. The container will listen on port 80, and we create a link to the **grafana** container so that this container can resolve the hostname **grafana** to the Grafana container’s IP address.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Configure auth proxy authentication",
        "Full walkthrough using Docker.",
        "Apache Container"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-access/configure-authentication/auth-proxy/index.md",
