    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.0f280019f988ef9eca2c",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You should now see a Generic OAuth login button on the login page and be able to log in or sign up with your OAuth2 provider.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Configure Generic OAuth authentication",
        "Configure generic OAuth authentication client using the Grafana configuration file",
        "Steps"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-access/configure-authentication/generic-oauth/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "996494cdc76551860001d5497ab4650b4563badf",
        "sha256": "93bacfb30c084c7dd0e225675e875cd091c4a0ef7a5053c330ccb6c9cd367d87",
        "lineStart": 127,
        "lineEnd": 127,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-access/configure-authentication/generic-oauth/index.md#L127-L127"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.a1931b104aefb0fcfd2d",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Grafana can resolve a user's login from the OAuth2 ID token, user information retrieved from the OAuth2 UserInfo endpoint, or the OAuth2 access token. Grafana looks at these sources in the order listed until it finds a login. If no login is found, then the user's login is set to user's email address.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Configure Generic OAuth authentication",
        "Configure generic OAuth authentication client using the Grafana configuration file",
        "Configure login"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-access/configure-authentication/generic-oauth/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "996494cdc76551860001d5497ab4650b4563badf",
        "sha256": "93bacfb30c084c7dd0e225675e875cd091c4a0ef7a5053c330ccb6c9cd367d87",
        "lineStart": 131,
        "lineEnd": 133,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-access/configure-authentication/generic-oauth/index.md#L131-L133"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.91955c7989e4262dc115",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Email is required for successful sign-up and login with Generic OAuth. Even if you map `login` from another claim (for example `sub`), Grafana still requires the user to have an email. Ensure your provider returns an email claim or configure `email_attribute_path` so Grafana can resolve it. Including the `email` scope is strongly recommended (for OIDC providers use `openid profile email`).",
      "headingPath": [
        "Configure Generic OAuth authentication",
        "Configure generic OAuth authentication client using the Grafana configuration file",
        "Configure login"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-access/configure-authentication/generic-oauth/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "996494cdc76551860001d5497ab4650b4563badf",
        "sha256": "93bacfb30c084c7dd0e225675e875cd091c4a0ef7a5053c330ccb6c9cd367d87",
        "lineStart": 136,
        "lineEnd": 136,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-access/configure-authentication/generic-oauth/index.md#L136-L136"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.78f70eb9f77f0024bcdc",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Refer to the following table for information on what to configure based on how your Oauth2 provider returns a user's login:",
