    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.5e10e366d149cfc35508",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "SCIM provisioning works in conjunction with existing user management methods in Grafana. While SCIM automates user provisioning from the identity provider, users can still be created through SAML just-in-time provisioning when they log in, manually through the Grafana UI, or via automation tools like Terraform and the Grafana API. For the most consistent user management experience, we recommend centralizing user provisioning through SCIM.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Manage users and teams with SCIM",
        "User provisioning with SCIM"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-access/configure-scim-provisioning/manage-users-teams/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "f199fd8464465d2c3724dfde2bec7672d4adfe15",
        "sha256": "3f0b7da5b83f963a73b37a94d6acbbe62d7dacc78677479c7b66ca10017ae367",
        "lineStart": 39,
        "lineEnd": 39,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-access/configure-scim-provisioning/manage-users-teams/_index.md#L39-L39"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-explicit-document-products",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.e169cea711342ec9677f",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "User provisioning requires `user_sync_enabled = true` in the SCIM configuration. See [Configure SCIM in Grafana](../../configure-scim-provisioning#configure-scim-in-grafana) for more information.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Manage users and teams with SCIM",
        "User provisioning with SCIM"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-access/configure-scim-provisioning/manage-users-teams/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "f199fd8464465d2c3724dfde2bec7672d4adfe15",
        "sha256": "3f0b7da5b83f963a73b37a94d6acbbe62d7dacc78677479c7b66ca10017ae367",
        "lineStart": 42,
        "lineEnd": 42,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-access/configure-scim-provisioning/manage-users-teams/_index.md#L42-L42"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-explicit-document-products",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.41fa61ed482ca6bdddd5",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "After a user is provisioned through SCIM, they cannot be deleted from Grafana - they can only be deactivated through the identity provider. This is important to consider when planning your user management strategy, especially for compliance and data retention requirements.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Manage users and teams with SCIM",
        "User provisioning with SCIM"
      ],
      "source": {
