    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.95c85dc7b2b80b825b66",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can install publicly available plugins and plugins that are private or used internally in an organization. For plugin installation instructions, refer to [Install plugins in the Docker container](../installation/docker/#install-plugins-in-the-docker-container).",
      "headingPath": [
        "Configure a Grafana Docker image",
        "Install plugins in the Docker container"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-docker.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "d91b83cf21311b97e3e286b7c1efc686959b4b9f",
        "sha256": "c76f5bf33aa9948420698d8a2f35a8495645f0e19c57f16743f2e31ec133f9a7",
        "lineStart": 131,
        "lineEnd": 131,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-docker.md#L131-L131"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.02c58b93aeecb6252438",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "To install plugins from other sources, you must define the custom URL and specify it immediately before the plugin name in the `GF_PLUGINS_PREINSTALL` environment variable: `GF_PLUGINS_PREINSTALL=<plugin ID>@[<plugin version>]@<url to plugin zip>`.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Configure a Grafana Docker image",
        "Install plugins in the Docker container",
        "Install plugins from other sources"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-docker.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "d91b83cf21311b97e3e286b7c1efc686959b4b9f",
        "sha256": "c76f5bf33aa9948420698d8a2f35a8495645f0e19c57f16743f2e31ec133f9a7",
        "lineStart": 135,
        "lineEnd": 135,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-docker.md#L135-L135"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.4ee3e2e74952b7992333",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "In the Grafana GitHub repository, the `packaging/docker/custom/` folder includes a `Dockerfile` that you can use to build a custom Grafana image. The `Dockerfile` accepts `GRAFANA_VERSION` and `GF_INSTALL_PLUGINS` as build arguments.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Configure a Grafana Docker image",
        "Build a custom Grafana Docker image"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-docker.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "d91b83cf21311b97e3e286b7c1efc686959b4b9f",
        "sha256": "c76f5bf33aa9948420698d8a2f35a8495645f0e19c57f16743f2e31ec133f9a7",
        "lineStart": 149,
        "lineEnd": 149,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-docker.md#L149-L149"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.3c3992a36f3882d83018",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The `GRAFANA_VERSION` build argument must be a valid `grafana/grafana` Docker image tag. By default, Grafana builds an Alpine-based image. To build an Ubuntu-based image, append `-ubuntu` to the `GRAFANA_VERSION` build argument.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Configure a Grafana Docker image",
        "Build a custom Grafana Docker image"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-docker.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "d91b83cf21311b97e3e286b7c1efc686959b4b9f",
        "sha256": "c76f5bf33aa9948420698d8a2f35a8495645f0e19c57f16743f2e31ec133f9a7",
        "lineStart": 151,
        "lineEnd": 151,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-docker.md#L151-L151"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.60611b8d31edb8cfc76b",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "If you run multiple Grafana installations with the same plugins, you can save time by building a customized image that includes plugins available on the [Grafana Plugin download page](/grafana/plugins). When you build a customized image, Grafana doesn't have to install the plugins each time it starts, making the startup process more efficient.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Configure a Grafana Docker image",
        "Build a custom Grafana Docker image",
        "Build a Grafana Docker image with pre-installed plugins"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-docker.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "d91b83cf21311b97e3e286b7c1efc686959b4b9f",
        "sha256": "c76f5bf33aa9948420698d8a2f35a8495645f0e19c57f16743f2e31ec133f9a7",
        "lineStart": 172,
        "lineEnd": 172,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-docker.md#L172-L172"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.253f6f019ed2104753b3",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "> **Note:** To specify the version of a plugin, you can use the `GF_INSTALL_PLUGINS` build argument and add the version number. The latest version is used if you don't specify a version number. For example, you can use `--build-arg \"GF_INSTALL_PLUGINS=grafana-clock-panel 1.0.1,yesoreyeram-infinity-datasource 3.8.0\"` to specify the versions of two plugins.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Configure a Grafana Docker image",
        "Build a custom Grafana Docker image",
        "Build a Grafana Docker image with pre-installed plugins"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-docker.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "d91b83cf21311b97e3e286b7c1efc686959b4b9f",
        "sha256": "c76f5bf33aa9948420698d8a2f35a8495645f0e19c57f16743f2e31ec133f9a7",
        "lineStart": 174,
        "lineEnd": 174,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-docker.md#L174-L174"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.ea31b67b84eb951fc415",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can create a Docker image containing a plugin that is exclusive to your organization, even if it is not accessible to the public. Simply use the `GF_INSTALL_PLUGINS` build argument to specify the plugin's URL and installation folder name, such as `GF_INSTALL_PLUGINS=<url to plugin zip>;<plugin install folder name>`.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Configure a Grafana Docker image",
        "Build a custom Grafana Docker image",
