      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.6116a0651fc09956b2fa",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Only available for the HTTP client. Disabled by default. How long to wait before sending a request to Loki with the batch of events. Uses duration format: e.g. 5s, 1m Whichever threshold is hit first between `batch_wait_duration` and `batch_size_bytes` triggers the batch to be sent to Loki. If the wait duration is very long and the `batch_size_bytes` is very high, events might take a long time to be sent. To enable batching, you must also set the `batch_size_bytes` configuration option.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Configure Grafana Enterprise",
        "[auditing.logs.loki]",
        "batch_wait_duration"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-grafana/enterprise-configuration/index.md",
