    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.add784f0fadbba8a4193",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You use feature toggles, also known as feature flags, to enable or disable features in Grafana. You can turn on feature toggles to try out new functionality in development or test environments.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Configure feature toggles"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-grafana/feature-toggles/index.md",
