    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.e28a505b2c6311be6481",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "By default, dashboard content doesn't appear in audit logs because it can significantly increase log size. To include dashboard content, enable the `log_dashboard_content` option.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Audit a Grafana instance",
        "Configure audit logging"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-security/audit-grafana.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "a9fcf3dc960f2d43a8ec00029c536b2c8f420635",
        "sha256": "b6963213d04b5904eb5810639906d3d281e3b6eed681456732071846799d65f2",
        "lineStart": 371,
        "lineEnd": 371,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-security/audit-grafana.md#L371-L371"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-explicit-document-products",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.1f0af7ccd7bd2f8b2ed1",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Data source query request and response bodies are also excluded by default. Enabling `log_datasource_query_request_body` or `log_datasource_query_response_body` significantly increases log volume and may expose sensitive data such as query parameters, credentials, or personally identifiable information.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Audit a Grafana instance",
        "Configure audit logging"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-security/audit-grafana.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "a9fcf3dc960f2d43a8ec00029c536b2c8f420635",
        "sha256": "b6963213d04b5904eb5810639906d3d281e3b6eed681456732071846799d65f2",
        "lineStart": 373,
        "lineEnd": 373,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-security/audit-grafana.md#L373-L373"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-explicit-document-products",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.154e35b4c89df0a276eb",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Before Grafana serves `DELETE /api/admin/users/{id}`, it tries to capture the user's display name, or login when the display name is empty, so the audit log can retain it after a successful deletion. The `snapshot_timeout` option sets a cooperative context deadline for this lookup. The user store must honor context cancellation, so the setting isn't a strict upper bound on request latency. If the lookup fails or observes an expired deadline, Grafana continues to process the request. If the deletion succeeds, the audit log omits `resources[x].name`.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Audit a Grafana instance",
        "Configure audit logging"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/setup-grafana/configure-security/audit-grafana.md",
