    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.da44b4762a6aede198bc",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- In a dashboard, you can build a graph panel with the queries `sum by(host) (count_over_time({kind=\"usage_insights\"} | json | eventName=\"data-request\" | error != \"\" [$__interval]))` and `sum by(host) (count_over_time({kind=\"usage_insights\"} | json | eventName=\"data-request\" | error = \"\" [$__interval]))` to show the evolution of the data request count over time. Using `by (host)` allows you to have more information for each Grafana server you have if you have set up Grafana for [high availability](../../set-up-for-high-availability/).",
      "headingPath": [
        "Export logs of usage insights",
