    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.5b82f0bb9f8b6b62c185",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Some features might require more memory or CPUs. For more information, refer to the following sizing guidance.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Install Grafana",
        "Hardware recommendations"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/setup-grafana/installation/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "0375272bc13891108a61af95a43d5fdbb29272d4",
        "sha256": "d47c19597705e01e7f35bb165ea58a752edc5fc63824e8ae3ba55574a5cf4adb",
        "lineStart": 51,
        "lineEnd": 51,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/setup-grafana/installation/_index.md#L51-L51"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.3d19551e3e032f18926b",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "This sizing guidance covers the Grafana server process only, meaning the UI, data source proxy, alert engine, and image renderer. It does not account for the resources required by your data sources. Metric stores such as Prometheus or Grafana Mimir, log stores such as Grafana Loki, and trace backends such as Grafana Tempo each have their own hardware and capacity requirements. For guidance, refer to [Planning Grafana Mimir capacity](https://grafana.com/docs/mimir/latest/manage/run-production-environment/planning-capacity), [Size the Loki cluster](https://grafana.com/docs/loki/latest/setup/size), and [Plan your Tempo deployment](https://grafana.com/docs/tempo/latest/set-up-for-tracing/setup-tempo/plan/).",
      "headingPath": [
        "Install Grafana",
        "Hardware recommendations",
        "Sizing your deployment"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/setup-grafana/installation/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "0375272bc13891108a61af95a43d5fdbb29272d4",
        "sha256": "d47c19597705e01e7f35bb165ea58a752edc5fc63824e8ae3ba55574a5cf4adb",
        "lineStart": 55,
        "lineEnd": 55,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/setup-grafana/installation/_index.md#L55-L55"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.94761fd1508236564b0f",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- **Concurrent users:** active, concurrent browser sessions issuing queries or causing panels to refresh. This is the primary driver of CPU and memory load. Users who have Grafana open but are not actively viewing dashboards contribute little load, unless those dashboards have auto-refresh enabled.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Install Grafana",
        "Hardware recommendations",
        "Sizing your deployment"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/setup-grafana/installation/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "0375272bc13891108a61af95a43d5fdbb29272d4",
        "sha256": "d47c19597705e01e7f35bb165ea58a752edc5fc63824e8ae3ba55574a5cf4adb",
        "lineStart": 59,
        "lineEnd": 59,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/setup-grafana/installation/_index.md#L59-L59"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.3c69625e99ffdb84ea7b",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- **Alert rules:** background evaluation load on the alert scheduler. High rule counts with short evaluation intervals can saturate CPU independently of user activity. In Grafana OSS, the alert engine runs in the same process as the UI and data source proxy, so alert CPU saturation directly competes with dashboard query performance. This is why isolating alert evaluation to dedicated instances matters at Large scale. Refer to [Performance considerations and limitations](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/<GRAFANA_VERSION>/alerting/set-up/performance-limitations/) for details.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Install Grafana",
        "Hardware recommendations",
        "Sizing your deployment"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/setup-grafana/installation/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "0375272bc13891108a61af95a43d5fdbb29272d4",
        "sha256": "d47c19597705e01e7f35bb165ea58a752edc5fc63824e8ae3ba55574a5cf4adb",
        "lineStart": 60,
        "lineEnd": 60,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/setup-grafana/installation/_index.md#L60-L60"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.162698e336d57ce0ffeb",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- **Data sources:** while the number of proxied data source connections matters, type matters more. Plugins that use the Grafana backend data source proxy — most SQL sources such as MySQL, PostgreSQL, and Microsoft SQL Server — hold an open connection per query on the server. Pull-based metric sources such as Prometheus or Graphite are queried more efficiently and place less load on the Grafana process. Some plugins, such as certain public API or Infinity sources, execute queries directly in the browser and may place no server-side load — depending on plugin configuration and authentication requirements. A deployment with five heavily-queried proxied SQL data sources can exceed the resource needs of one with twenty Prometheus sources.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Install Grafana",
        "Hardware recommendations",
        "Sizing your deployment"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/setup-grafana/installation/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "0375272bc13891108a61af95a43d5fdbb29272d4",
        "sha256": "d47c19597705e01e7f35bb165ea58a752edc5fc63824e8ae3ba55574a5cf4adb",
        "lineStart": 61,
        "lineEnd": 61,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/setup-grafana/installation/_index.md#L61-L61"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.ce0011314c736913b618",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- **Dashboards and panels:** panel count and refresh interval together determine query throughput. A dashboard with 30 panels refreshing every 10 seconds generates roughly six times the query load of the same dashboard refreshing every minute. Dashboards with many panels and short refresh intervals should be treated as a tier higher than their raw dashboard count suggests. Note that Grafana Enterprise includes query caching, which can significantly reduce this multiplier when many users view the same dashboard simultaneously and may shift a deployment down a tier.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Install Grafana",
        "Hardware recommendations",
        "Sizing your deployment"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/setup-grafana/installation/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "0375272bc13891108a61af95a43d5fdbb29272d4",
        "sha256": "d47c19597705e01e7f35bb165ea58a752edc5fc63824e8ae3ba55574a5cf4adb",
        "lineStart": 62,
        "lineEnd": 62,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/setup-grafana/installation/_index.md#L62-L62"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "mixed-edition-statement-requires-review",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.7e51d4d34aa5daeaf40e",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Image rendering and large numbers of short-interval alert rules are the two most common reasons a deployment outgrows its initial sizing. Multi-organization setups and SSO or LDAP directory sync add overhead that can push a deployment into the next tier.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Install Grafana",
        "Hardware recommendations",
        "Sizing your deployment"
      ],
