    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.ec22571c5f452ba79974",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Grafana supports Debian and Ubuntu, RHEL and Fedora, SUSE and openSUSE, macOS, and Windows. You can also run Grafana in a container with Docker or deploy it on Kubernetes with the Grafana Helm chart. Installing Grafana on other operating systems is possible but is neither recommended nor supported. For platform-specific steps, refer to the installation guide for your operating system.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Install Grafana",
        "Frequently asked questions"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/setup-grafana/installation/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "0375272bc13891108a61af95a43d5fdbb29272d4",
        "sha256": "d47c19597705e01e7f35bb165ea58a752edc5fc63824e8ae3ba55574a5cf4adb",
        "lineStart": 182,
        "lineEnd": 185,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/setup-grafana/installation/_index.md#L182-L185"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.bfa6c2d12f4b19e28565",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "At a minimum, Grafana needs 512 MB of memory and 1 CPU core, but that's a floor for evaluation rather than a production target. Actual requirements are driven by four factors: concurrent users, the number of alert rules and how often they evaluate, the number and type of data sources, and your panel count and dashboard refresh intervals. The documentation groups workloads into Small, Medium, and Large tiers with a hardware baseline for each. For example, a small deployment starts at 2 cores and 2–4 GB of memory, while a large deployment runs multiple load-balanced instances at 8–16+ cores and 16–32+ GB of memory each. This guidance covers the Grafana server process only. It doesn't account for your data sources, because metric, log, and trace backends such as Grafana Mimir, Grafana Loki, and Grafana Tempo have their own capacity requirements. Treat the tiers as starting points and validate them with a load test that reflects your real dashboards before you commit to production hardware. For more information, refer to Sizing your deployment.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Install Grafana",
        "Frequently asked questions"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/setup-grafana/installation/_index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "0375272bc13891108a61af95a43d5fdbb29272d4",
        "sha256": "d47c19597705e01e7f35bb165ea58a752edc5fc63824e8ae3ba55574a5cf4adb",
        "lineStart": 188,
        "lineEnd": 195,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/setup-grafana/installation/_index.md#L188-L195"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
