    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.32d7472e8469000deed9",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "By default, Grafana uses an embedded SQLite version 3 database to store configuration, users, dashboards, and other data. When you run Docker images as containers, changes to these Grafana data are written to the filesystem within the container, which will only persist for as long as the container exists. If you stop and remove the container, any filesystem changes (i.e. the Grafana data) will be discarded. To avoid losing your data, you can set up persistent storage using [Docker volumes](https://docs.docker.com/storage/volumes/) or [bind mounts](https://docs.docker.com/storage/bind-mounts/) for your container.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Run Grafana Docker image",
        "Run Grafana via Docker CLI",
        "Save your Grafana data"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/setup-grafana/installation/docker/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "4775409c5b7e8b32342ff84f543f3e11c51aa950",
        "sha256": "d22215b5401d2dbb28e4e78cd75823626dbed0af66963f21c05477a85dc715a9",
        "lineStart": 74,
        "lineEnd": 74,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/setup-grafana/installation/docker/index.md#L74-L74"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.2295c5f00826067211d4",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "> **Note:** Though both methods are similar, there is a slight difference. If you want your storage to be fully managed by Docker and accessed only through Docker containers and the Docker CLI, you should choose to use persistent storage. However, if you need full control of the storage and want to allow other processes besides Docker to access or modify the storage layer, then bind mounts is the right choice for your environment.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Run Grafana Docker image",
        "Run Grafana via Docker CLI",
        "Save your Grafana data"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/setup-grafana/installation/docker/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "4775409c5b7e8b32342ff84f543f3e11c51aa950",
        "sha256": "d22215b5401d2dbb28e4e78cd75823626dbed0af66963f21c05477a85dc715a9",
        "lineStart": 76,
        "lineEnd": 76,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/setup-grafana/installation/docker/index.md#L76-L76"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.c851b70fbe9290ab5819",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Use Docker volumes when you want the Docker Engine to manage the storage volume.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Run Grafana Docker image",
        "Run Grafana via Docker CLI",
        "Save your Grafana data",
        "Use Docker volumes (recommended)"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/setup-grafana/installation/docker/index.md",
